  "body": {
    "id": "lem:finite-design-attainable-quantile",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For each fixed \\(N\\) and allowed observed design, \\(\\Lambda_N^{\\mathrm{phys}}\\) is compact.  The law of\n\\[\n d_{H_N}(G_N+\\lambda q_N(p),\\mathcal C_N)^2\n\\]\nis atomless and has a strictly increasing distribution function on \\((0,\\infty)\\); its \\((1-\\alpha)\\)-quantile is continuous in \\((\\lambda,p)\\).  Hence the maximum defining \\(c_{N,\\alpha}^{\\mathrm{att}}\\) is attained and\n\\[\n \\inf_{(\\lambda,p)\\in\\Lambda_N^{\\mathrm{phys}}}\n \\Pr\\{d_{H_N}(G_N+\\lambda q_N(p),\\mathcal C_N)^2\n       \\le c_{N,\\alpha}^{\\mathrm{att}}\\}=1-\\alpha.                           \\tag{20}\n\\]\nMoreover,\n\\[\n 0<c_{N,\\alpha}^{\\mathrm{att}}\\le\\chi^2_{2,1-\\alpha},                       \\tag{21}\n\\]\nand both bounds are uniform over the allowed designs after compactification.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "N",
      "design",
      "level",
      "lambda",
      "p",
      "qcurve",
      "H",
      "cone",
      "G",
      "Lambdaphys",
